<https://w3id.org/plato#FindspotOf> <https://w3id.org/plato#relation_domain> "SpatialEntity" .
<https://w3id.org/plato#start_latest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Literal> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#LeadsTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        A directed connection, from the subject (attests_about) to the target\n        (relates_to): one river flowing into another, a post road carrying\n        mail from one town to the next, letters sent from one city to\n        another. It joins two places; the reaches and legs of a network are\n        segments, whose direction is given by plato:BeginsAt and\n        plato:EndsAt. Not river-specific: a project declares its own narrower types ('flows\n        into', 'carries post to') with plato:broader_relation pointing here,\n        so that a consumer that knows only LeadsTo still follows them in the\n        right direction.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/bibliographicCitation> "Gadd, Stephen, and the Pelagios Network Place Working Group. PLATO — Place Attestation Ontology, version 0.7.1. Zenodo, 2026. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21688313" .
<https://w3id.org/plato#has_timespan> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/plato> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        The semantic strength of the identity assertion:\n        'exactMatch'  — the two SpatialEntities are unambiguously the same entity.\n        'closeMatch'  — the two SpatialEntities are believed to be the same entity\n                        but with some residual ambiguity (e.g. differing\n                        granularity, overlapping but not identical scope).\n        'related'     — the two SpatialEntities are closely associated but may not\n                        be strictly identical (e.g. a settlement and its\n                        administrative district, or successive phases of\n                        a site that might or might not constitute continuity).\n        'unspecified' — the source links the two but does not say how strongly;\n                        honest where the alternative is to guess a strength.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#spatial_coverage> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
