<https://w3id.org/plato#TranscriptionAccuracyScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Starter concepts for plato:transcription_accuracy. How faithfully a transcribed value renders what the source shows."@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#start_latest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "start latest"@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#start_precision> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Temporal granularity of the start bound. Values: 'day', 'month',\n        'year', 'decade', 'century', 'era', 'geological_period' (as the\n        JSON Schema's precision enumeration). This describes the resolution\n        of the date specification, distinct from certainty (which describes\n        the confidence in that specification).\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#name_embedding> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Vector embedding for phonetic similarity search: a vector generated\n        from the name's phonetic form, enabling fuzzy matching and\n        transliteration-variant detection. Its model and dimension are the\n        producer's (WHG v4 uses Symphonym embeddings), so both must be\n        stated in the gazetteer's description: vectors from different\n        models cannot be compared.\n    "@en .
