<https://w3id.org/plato#Type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        A classification or category for a SpatialEntity, typically drawn from a\n        controlled vocabulary such as the Getty Art & Architecture Thesaurus\n        (AAT), as one dataset uses it. A Type node stands for that usage and\n        may be reused within its dataset. Its IRI, if it has one, is the\n        dataset's own, or it is a blank node: never the vocabulary concept's\n        IRI, which goes in plato:type_identifier. Otherwise every dataset's\n        label, source wording and plato:scheme_version would merge onto the\n        concept in any combined graph.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#language> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Name> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#partOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/plato#Dataset> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#Source> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        A citable source of evidence: a manuscript, chronicle, tax record,\n        map, scholarly article, or other document. Sources are the primary\n        provenance anchor for attestations. A Source may reference its parent\n        Dataset via plato:partOf.\n\n        A Source's licence, that of the edition or copy cited, is given with\n        dcterms:license, as a Gazetteer's is. A project that admits evidence\n        by its licence (citing a share-alike source as a witness but never\n        copying it, say) needs the licence on the thing cited, so that it\n        travels with the data.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_name> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#value_literal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "value"@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#SourceStanceScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Starter concepts for plato:source_stance. How firmly the source itself asserts what an attestation records, as distinct from anyone's confidence in it."@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#source_label> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#relation_domain> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#RelationType> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#Beyond> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "On the far side of the anchor from the point of view of the source."@en .
