<https://w3id.org/plato#value_type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        URI declaring the shape of a structured value, so that a consumer can\n        tell whether it understands the value before attempting to read it.\n        Omitted for literal values.\n\n        Not every attribute a source states is scalar. A market's trading day\n        — 'the Monday after Whitsun, for three days' — is a recurrence rule\n        anchored to a moveable feast, and flattening it to a string would\n        reproduce the loss this class exists to prevent. The ontology stays\n        agnostic about such shapes: it records which shape is in use and\n        leaves the definition to the vocabulary that owns it.\n    "@en .
