<https://w3id.org/plato#GazetteerGroup> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        A thematic or organisational grouping of Gazetteers (e.g.\n        'EMEW — Gazetteer of Early Modern England and Wales').\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#keyword> "provenance"@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#has_meta_type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#derived_from> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        This Source is a copy, transcript, edition, calendar or confirmation\n        of that one. A later cartulary copy of a charter, an inspeximus, or a\n        printed edition of a manuscript is a Source of its own, with its own\n        source_timespan, derived_from the document it transmits. An\n        attestation should cite the Source it was actually read in; the chain\n        of derived_from links records what that Source transmits. The kind of\n        derivation (copy, edition, calendar, inspeximus) is not yet\n        distinguished; a sub-property or a small vocabulary can be added when\n        a project needs it.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#property_type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        URI of the property in an external vocabulary — a Wikidata property,\n        a CIDOC-CRM property, or a project vocabulary term (e.g.\n        <https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Property:P1082> for population).\n        Keeping the vocabulary external rather than enumerating attributes in\n        this ontology is what allows the model to carry attributes it has\n        never heard of.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#IdentityRelation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Identity Relation"@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#name_embedding> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Name> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#citation_function> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#attests_type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/plato> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#Contradicts> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#Extent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The built or bounded extent of the SpatialEntity."@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#ContainedIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/plato#RelationType> .
