<https://w3id.org/plato#meta_attestation_about> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Links a meta-Attestation to the Attestation it comments on or relates to.\n        Used with plato:has_meta_type to specify the nature of the relationship.\n        A meta-attestation need not carry plato:attests_about: it is about its\n        target, and through it about the target's SpatialEntity. Where it does\n        carry one (as when nested under a place in place-centric JSON), that\n        should be the target's.\n\n        Example: A meta-attestation might assert that one source's geometry\n        attestation contradicts another source's geometry attestation for the\n        same SpatialEntity.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#meta_attestation_about> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
