<https://w3id.org/plato#attribution_status> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Citation> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#fuzziness> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Ontological fuzziness: a measure of how inherently vague or\n        indeterminate the facet's referent is, from 0.0 (crisp, sharply\n        bounded) to 1.0 (maximally vague). Distinct from certainty:\n        fuzziness is a property of the thing itself, not of our knowledge\n        of it. A regional boundary that was never precisely defined has\n        high fuzziness regardless of how much evidence we have.\n    "@en .
_:na519a30634a746a18aecd69d7dc797e5b9 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <https://w3id.org/plato#Name> .
