<https://w3id.org/plato#TranscriptionInaccurate> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#MemberOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        The subject is a member of the target route, itinerary or network: a\n        station on a road, a stop on a journey, a port in a trade network, a\n        segment of a river system. Its position, where the source gives one,\n        is plato:sequence on the same attestation. A route may be a member of\n        another route (one stage of a pilgrimage), but not, through any chain\n        of memberships, of itself. Not containment: a town on a road is not\n        within it, and a network's members need not lie inside anything.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#FindspotOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The target object (a coin, an inscription, a manuscript) was found at the subject. The timespan is when it was found, if known."@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_object> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#value_json> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "structured value"@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#value_unit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
