<https://w3id.org/plato#source_timespan> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        When this Source, as a document, was produced: the date of the\n        manuscript, the compilation of the cartulary, the publication of the\n        edition. Distinct from the Timespan an attestation asserts, which\n        dates the claim rather than the witness. An annal for 921 read in a\n        manuscript written c. 925 has an attested timespan of 921 and a\n        source timespan of c. 925. Reuses Timespan, so an approximate date\n        is start_earliest 915, end_latest 935, timespan_label 'c. 925'. The\n        same move as plato:has_timespan on a Period.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#citation_function> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#StanceAsserted> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The source states it as so, on its own account. The default source stance, usually omitted."@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#DeathplaceOf> <https://w3id.org/plato#relation_label> "deathplace_of" .
