<https://w3id.org/plato#Contradicts> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/plato> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#VariantOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/plato#RelativeQualifierScheme> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#DerivedFrom> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/plato#MetaTypeScheme> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#Authority> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#cites> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#attests_identity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Links an Attestation to an IdentityRelation it asserts, so that\n        identity relations asserted in one act share its provenance: accepting\n        a cluster of n records is one attestation bundling the n-1 exactMatch\n        relations of the matches actually made, with the person, the time and\n        the cluster's definition as its source. Retracting or superseding the\n        attestation withdraws or amends them together. With plato:negated,\n        bundling one exactMatch relation, it says the two entities are not the\n        same. Closure may be taken within one such attestation only (see\n        plato:IdentityRelation). An IdentityRelation's own identity_asserted_by\n        and identity_sourced_by remain for one asserted on its own.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#Authority> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/plato> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#Extent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "extent"@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#Within> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/plato#RelativeQualifierScheme> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#has_timespan> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/plato#Timespan> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#occurrence_context> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/plato> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#TranscriptionReconstructable> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/plato#TranscriptionCompletenessScheme> .
