<https://w3id.org/plato#ccodes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 codes of the modern countries whose territory\n        contains or overlaps this SpatialEntity, as in Linked Places Format.\n        A finding aid for search and matching, like a label: not evidence,\n        and not a claim about the past, so it needs no source. Where a\n        country is itself the subject of a historical claim (\"this town lay\n        in the Kingdom of Aragon\"), record it as a relation attestation.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#DepictedIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/plato#RelationType> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#publisher> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#type_label> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#Near> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Close to the anchor, without a stated bearing or distance."@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#Citation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Citation"@en .
