<https://w3id.org/plato#attribution_status> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Whether the attribution of the evidence to the cited source was\n        stated by the source or resolved editorially. Should point to a\n        concept in a SKOS concept scheme. The starter concepts are:\n\n        - plato:AttributionStated: the source is named where the form\n          occurs. The default, and usually omitted.\n        - plato:AttributionInferred: the source was given as 'ibidem' or\n          'idem' and resolved by an editor, so the attribution is inferred\n          rather than stated. Not marginal: about one attestation in twenty\n          in the English Place-Name Society corpus.\n\n        A statement about the citation, not about the form, which is why it\n        lives here and not in plato:occurrence_context.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#Period> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        A named historical period (e.g. 'Byzantine', 'Early Modern'),\n        optionally linked to PeriodO or defined locally. Includes temporal\n        bounds for period-based querying.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#sequence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contains_entity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#modified> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#StanceReported> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "reported"@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#modified> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "modified"@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#Geometry> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        A spatial representation of a SpatialEntity's extent or location. Geometries\n        are independent, reusable entities. The same Geometry may be referenced\n        by multiple Attestations across different SpatialEntities or time periods.\n\n        Each Geometry is one GeoJSON geometry; a GeometryCollection is not\n        accepted, so a set of different kinds (a point and a polygon) is\n        several Geometry nodes. One attestation may attest several\n        geometries when one source gives them all, each with a\n        plato:geometry_role where they depict different things (a built\n        extent, a label position); a geometry from another source is\n        another attestation, since it has another provenance. See\n        examples/geometry-roles.ttl.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#CertaintyLevel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_object> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/plato> .
