<https://w3id.org/plato#attests_property> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/plato> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#Direct> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The form refers to the SpatialEntity directly. The default occurrence context, usually omitted."@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#Retracts> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The target attestation is withdrawn: it no longer holds, and is kept only so that earlier states of the gazetteer can be reproduced. For a claim its maker takes back, such as a bad import, where plato:Contradicts would read as one scholar disputing another. A tool showing the current state leaves a retracted attestation out. A retraction is itself an attestation: retracting it withdraws the withdrawal, and the target holds again."@en .
