<https://w3id.org/plato#transcription_accuracy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        How faithfully a transcribed value (a name form, most often) renders\n        what the source shows: a concept in plato:TranscriptionAccuracyScheme,\n        plato:TranscriptionAccurate, plato:TranscriptionInaccurate or\n        plato:TranscriptionFalse. It judges the reading, not the source and not\n        the identification: plato:form_status says how a form came to be, and\n        plato:certainty how sure anyone is of the attestation, and neither says\n        how well the form was read. Pleiades records it for every name.\n\n        Like the other qualification properties it has no rdfs:domain, so a\n        transcribed coordinate or date can be judged the same way.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#declares_relation_type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "declares relation type"@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#certainty_note> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_email> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Contact email address for the contributor. Useful for collaboration\n        and correspondence about contributed data.\n    "@en .
