<https://w3id.org/plato#entity_identifier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        An identifier for this SpatialEntity other than its IRI: the\n        contributing project's own record id ('GLOB_366') or an authority's\n        ('geonames:2654675'), with plato:namespace saying whose. A finding aid,\n        like a label: not a claim about the place.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#licence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Deprecated: use dcterms:license. It could be given only to a Dataset,\n        it had no route in PLATO JSON, and it was a literal where a\n        Gazetteer's dcterms:license points at the licence itself. So the\n        licence of a cited source had no way into the data. dcterms:license has\n        no domain, so it serves every Authority and the Gazetteer alike, and\n        says nothing about what kind of thing is licensed. Kept for one release\n        under the deprecation policy.\n    "@en .
